Clear the loose ends that did not need Forrest, and say which ones did

Four done, one staged a command short, one blocked.

DONE. The honeypot key finally matches the field name. Book Prep and Checkout
Prep now accept nlma_check or the old company_website, the same way Guard
already did, and with all three accepting both, the page switched to posting
nlma_check. The trap this closes was real: the body key and the DOM field had
drifted apart, so the next person to rename one would have silently disabled
spam filtering with no test failing. The checkout call now sends the honeypot
too; it previously sent none at all, which made Checkout Prep's check dead code.
Old cached pages keep working. That is the last piece of nlma.io#4.

DONE. doneStep is gone. It was a "You're booked" card from before both paths
went through Stripe, referenced exactly once, only ever to hide it. Took the
stale #doneMsg mention in the CSS comment with it.

DONE. nlma.io#5 closed as completed, with a comment recording what actually
shipped: option 2 was built rather than the disclosure hidden, so the $112.50
the page promises now has a collection point behind it. The comment is honest
about the CSP half being staged and about the paid branch still never having
run.

STAGED, ONE COMMAND SHORT. The CSP now carries form-action 'self'
https://checkout.stripe.com and has dropped the inert frame-src for
calendar.google.com, since the Google Calendar iframe was replaced by the custom
picker. nginx -t passes and there is a timestamped backup. The reload did not
run: the Shell MCP chroot is in a separate PID namespace, so nginx -s reload
dies with kill(...) No such process, and SSH from here was refused. Needs
systemctl reload nginx on the host. Nothing is broken meanwhile, and the
site does no form posts at all, so the old policy blocks nothing.

BLOCKED. The duplicated slot constants need a rewire, not just an edit. The real
fix is to make the intake path triage-only, since it computes availability that
nobody reads: the visitor already picked a time from /consult-slots. That would
delete HOURS, DOW, HORIZON and MINH from Parse+Slots, leave Slots Prep as the
single source, and drop a wasted freeBusy call on every intake. Code-only is not
an option, because changing the code without rewiring leaves FreeBusy with an
undefined timeMin. The structural n8n write was refused by the classifier, so it
is recorded with the reasoning instead of half-applied.

Also corrected in the doc: L4 says retire /consult-book AFTER item 1 passes, not
before. It is the rollback path, and retiring it first would remove the net
before the wire is tested.

